winewayland: on Plasma every tray menu is the application's own, opened at the click (his option B).

Patch 125 started a Plasma tray icon without the dbusmenu (so Plasma calls ContextMenu with the click point) and, once
its application showed a Win32 menu, re-registered the item with the dbusmenu so later right-clicks were drawn by
Plasma at the icon. The first menu then looked different from the later ones, and the re-registration could move the
icon once. His call (11-04): "Option b" -- on Plasma always show the application's own menu at the click, which is how
Windows shows tray menus (the application draws them). GNOME, XFCE and waybar keep the dbusmenu: their trays only offer
that.

The ContextMenu probe that triggered the switch is now opt-in (NEUTRON_TRAY_PLASMA_DBUSMENU=1 restores 125's behavior).
Nothing else changes: the menu is placed at the click by 125's layer surface.

Lab 180u (= 180 + 125 + this winewayland.so, both arches), nested Plasma 6 on desk E, traytest v4 (a Win32 menu):
right-click, Escape, right-click: both menus are the application's own window at the click ("menu at cursor
1896,1203"), Escape returns 0, the item is never re-announced, 2/2. NEUTRON_TRAY_PLASMA_DBUSMENU=1 on the same build:
"shows Win32 menus: the tray will draw", "announced again", the second right-click opens Plasma's menu, 1/1.

--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_sni.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_sni.c
@@ -245,6 +245,17 @@
     return kde && sni_dbusmenu_enabled() && wayland_tray_popup_layer_enabled();
 }
 
+/* NEUTRON tray-plasma-own-menu (his option B, 2026-11-04): on Plasma every tray menu is the application's own, opened at
+ * the click, as Windows shows tray menus (the application draws them). The ContextMenu probe that moved an icon to the
+ * dbusmenu after its first Win32 menu (Plasma-drawn menus from the second click on, a first menu that looked different,
+ * the icon re-registered and moving once) is opt-in: NEUTRON_TRAY_PLASMA_DBUSMENU=1. */
+static BOOL sni_kde_probe(void)
+{
+    static int on = -1;
+    if (on < 0) { const char *e = getenv( "NEUTRON_TRAY_PLASMA_DBUSMENU" ); on = e && e[0] == '1'; }
+    return on;
+}
+
 static ULONGLONG sni_ticks(void)
 {
     struct timespec ts;
@@ -662,7 +673,7 @@
         icon->last_click = sni_last_click = pt;
     }
     /* NEUTRON tray-menus-v2: a Win32 menu the application opens for this click tells us its kind (menu_offered) */
-    if (!strcmp( member, "ContextMenu" ) && !icon->use_dbusmenu && sni_kde_context())
+    if (!strcmp( member, "ContextMenu" ) && !icon->use_dbusmenu && sni_kde_context() && sni_kde_probe())
     {
         if (!(request = ++sni_menu_counter & 0xffff)) request = ++sni_menu_counter & 0xffff;
         icon->context_request = request;
